---------------------------------------
README file for OxInsIPS Support Module
---------------------------------------

This is the EPICS support module for the Oxford Instruments
Intelligent Power Supply series of power supplies, designed for
superconducting magnets.

The module was developed to support the Beamline I10 Absorption branch
BL10J Magnet End Station a.k.a. the High Field Magnet.

The fact that it is a modular power supply means that several units
can be linked together, but they function as one to deliver power and
also from a Controls point of view.

For example on the DLS BL10J Magnet, 2 units have been coupled together to
make a single power supply unit.

Oxford Instruments reflect this in the model number of what they
supply, so what appear to different models may in fact be similar
units chained together differently.

The power supply is now considered obsolete by the suppliers and there
was a problem with it in 2019 and a replacement was loaned to the
beamline with a view to purchase.  The firmware and protocol of the
new model, which has a different name.  The new model has a "legacy"
mode.  When placed in the legacy mode, the existing IOC communicated
with it with no further intervention.  However the comms setup
functionality does not work (but it is not required).

To use non-legacy mode, which has more functionality in it, further development
would be required.

Last updated 02/12/2019

